# WhatsApp Utility templates (Partner subscriptions)

Replaces WhatsApp on the catch-all `PartnerSubsParentUpdate` (moved to **Marketing** by Meta in Nov 2026) and the pending `PartnerSubsPodUpdate`. Those two rows stay for the **web inbox only**; WhatsApp now uses one template per kind of event. Code: `WA` in `subscription-checkout.notifications.ts`.

## Create each template (Twilio Content Template Builder)

- Type: **Call to action**, one **Visit website** button. Button URL = the same redirect base as the existing `PartnerSubsParentUpdate` button, followed by the last variable (the auto-login code). Language: English.
- Submit for WhatsApp approval as **Utility** with **Allow category change: off** (`allow_category_change: false`), so Meta rejects it instead of approving it as Marketing.
- Paste the body exactly; use the samples below. Variables are single-line text.
- Don't add promotional wording (offers, "join another pod", "explore").

## Turn one on (notice-tpl row)

Rows are seeded by `/addNoticeTpls` (`middleware/newNoticeForScript.ts`) switched off: inbox off, email off, `enableWaba: false`. After Meta approves a template, set its row's `wabaContentSid` to the Content SID and `enableWaba: true` (admin notice-tpl screen; saving clears the template cache). Until then that event is inbox only. Keep `wabaVars` exactly as listed (it maps names to {{1}}, {{2}}, …).

